WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.701
Logs and diagnostics often expose what source code avoided exposing.

2
00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:10.785
A team may carefully protect a token in memory and then print it during troubleshooting.

3
00:00:10.785 --> 00:00:18.045
A controller may avoid returning sensitive fields while telemetry captures them in a structured property.

4
00:00:18.045 --> 00:00:21.916
Operational output is part of the data handling surface.

5
00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:36.712
Sensitive data can leak through structured logs, HTTP logs, exception messages, stack traces, telemetry, traces, metrics labels, crash dumps, health checks, debug pages, support tickets, screenshots, and CI output.

6
00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:45.630
These systems often have different retention, access control, search, export, and sharing behavior than the application database.

7
00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:57.453
Do not log passwords, tokens, API keys, connection strings, authorization headers, cookies, reset links, raw personal data, raw financial data, or full sensitive payloads.

8
00:00:57.453 --> 00:01:07.063
When sensitive details are needed for a controlled investigation, use an approved evidence process rather than routine application logging.

9
00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:10.174
Error responses should be useful but limited.

10
00:01:10.174 --> 00:01:20.821
They should not reveal internal paths, schema details, stack traces, secret names, tenant identifiers, provider configuration, or raw exception internals.

11
00:01:20.821 --> 00:01:27.251
The user-facing response and the operator diagnostic record should serve different audiences.

12
00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:31.261
Redaction should be designed and tested before production.

13
00:01:31.261 --> 00:01:43.982
It should cover structured properties, message templates, exception details, HTTP headers, request bodies, response bodies, background job payloads, and dependency logs where relevant.

14
00:01:43.982 --> 00:01:50.550
A redaction policy that exists only as a code comment will not protect the system consistently.

15
00:01:50.550 --> 00:02:02.234
Useful logging preserves safe context: correlation ID, operation name, failure category, safe resource identifier, environment, dependency category, timing, and outcome.

16
00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:12.605
Production diagnostics should be access-controlled, environment-scoped, retained appropriately, and periodically reviewed for sensitive data exposure.
